WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.020
Your foot swings through
and strikes a ball.

2
00:00:03.070 --> 00:00:04.590
Then they part.

3
00:00:04.640 --> 00:00:08.920
Your foot stops, and the
ball sails on, up and away.

4
00:00:08.970 --> 00:00:11.850
It keeps moving long
after the kick is over.

5
00:00:11.900 --> 00:00:14.270
Something must still be acting on it.

6
00:00:14.320 --> 00:00:15.990
Or must it?

7
00:00:16.040 --> 00:00:20.570
With air resistance ignored, which forces
still act on the ball once it has left

8
00:00:20.620 --> 00:00:21.710
your foot?

9
00:00:21.760 --> 00:00:24.770
In this mission, you'll
meet the everyday forces:

10
00:00:24.820 --> 00:00:28.470
weight, normal force,
friction and tension.

11
00:00:28.520 --> 00:00:31.860
Then you'll draw free-body
diagrams: one object,

12
00:00:31.910 --> 00:00:34.360
with each force on it as an arrow.

13
00:00:34.410 --> 00:00:39.080
Your mission: find out which forces act
on the ball once it has left your foot.
